{"bbox":[156.672,194.832,421.668,382.536],"caption":"Figure 14: Error of the neural network classifier depending on the mixture coeficient a. Each poin of the plot corresponds to the average estimated coeficient by the neural network for all mixture surfaces with a given a. For example, for $a = 0$ , the surfaces are generated from the rough Bergomi model. For each parameter combination from those surfaces, we compute the predicted mixture coeficient and average all of them over the validation set to report ˆa. The network never sets the mixture coeficient very close to 1 or $0 ,$ attributing the surface to one specific model. This may be explained using Bayesian reasoning.","figure_id":"2019-horvath-et-al-deep-learning-volatility:p0028:figure:0001","page_number":28,"paper_id":"2019-horvath-et-al-deep-learning-volatility","provenance":{"extractor_name":"MinerU pipeline","extractor_version":"3.4.4","model_hash":"ed6b654c018d742e65a17671e379c5e6ecc87ec9","source_pdf_sha256":"ce59a01948af7b4e092e1c89dce0cca800d71888f286c50416ceea4388655332"},"source_asset":"assets/figures/2019-horvath-et-al-deep-learning-volatility-p0028-block-0003-cff1a6bbc235021e.jpg","source_bbox_normalized":[256,246,689,483],"source_block_id":"2019-horvath-et-al-deep-learning-volatility:p0028:block:0003","verification_status":"unverified"}
